# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .vercelignore — what must NOT be deployed.
#
# ⚠️ READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A FILE TO THE REPO.
#
# This project has no framework and no build output directory, so Vercel serves
# the git-tracked repo root directly as static files. That means
# ANYTHING COMMITTED IS FETCHABLE AT garagesalebiz.com/<path>, including files
# nothing links to. "Nothing links to it" is not privacy — it is a URL nobody has
# thought to try yet.
#
# EstateSaleBiz verified this the hard way: buyer-agreement.md and its full
# database schema, including RLS policy definitions, both returned 200 on the live
# site for weeks. Assume every new file is public until it is listed here.
#
# Uses .gitignore pattern syntax.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── DATABASE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The schema, every RLS policy, the storage rules, and the project reference.
# None of it is fetched by any page, and publishing it hands an attacker the
# complete map of what is protected and how.
*.sql

# ── INTERNAL DOCS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Setup runbooks naming env vars, dashboard steps, and the launch sequence.
# Never linked from a live page, and each one is a checklist of what to attack.
STRIPE-SETUP.md
BREVO-SETUP.md
LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md
README.md
*.md

# ── ARCHIVE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Abandoned waitlist work kept for history. Its migration targets a DIFFERENT
# Supabase project and must never run; serving it would be worse than pointless.
archive/

# ── THE MULTI-NICHE PAGE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# niches.html is the SystemsByVega umbrella storefront, preserved in git because
# it will live somewhere else later. It is excluded from THIS deployment for two
# reasons, and the second is the one that matters:
#
#   1. It is not part of GarageSaleBiz and belongs on a different domain.
#   2. Its content is now WRONG. It lists garage-and-moving-sales as
#      "waitlist" — a product that is live and on sale on this very domain. A
#      visitor who found it would be told they cannot buy the thing they can buy.
#
# Its script is excluded with it: waitlist.js writes to own_waitlist, a table that
# was never created and never will be in this project.
niches.html
waitlist.js

# ── EDITOR AND BACKUP SCRATCH ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A .bak of a page is a second verbatim copy of it at a URL nobody checks.
# Paired with .gitignore: that rule stops the commit, this one stops the deploy if
# something is ever force-added or was tracked before the ignore rule existed.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ── LOCAL TOOLING ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/

# ── NOT EXCLUDED, DELIBERATELY ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# course-data.js IS served. It is the course content, loaded as a plain <script>
# by course.html, and gating it behind authentication would mean an async refactor
# of that page for material that is educational rather than confidential. Anyone
# who wants it can already read it from a signed-in browser's network tab.
# Revisit only if the course is ever sold separately from a territory.
